// Position contract for overlay and label domains.
// x, y, fontSize, and icon width are pixels on the source artboard
// (4318×5400, origin at the top-left, y increasing downward — the same
// space as data/source/toronto-rising-map.svg). The map projects those
// pixels through data/calibration.json, so a point stays on its district
// while the player pans and zooms.
//
// Text: x,y is the center of the painted letters, including every line.
// In Photoshop, center-align the type, convert it to a smart object, trim
// it to its pixels, then read that object's center in the main document.
// Lines stay center-aligned and grow equally above and below that point.
// fontSize is the Character panel point size from before the conversion,
// not the smart object's width. The Photoshop master is 72 ppi at this
// artboard size, so that point size is already in artboard pixels. It
// scales with the map.
//
// Icons: x,y is the center of the graphic. width is the rendered width in
// artboard pixels; height follows the SVG. Place an icon under a label by
// giving it a larger y than the label.
//
// A placement of 0,0 with fontSize or width 0 is unfinished and is not drawn.
// Site domains do not use x,y. They name an existing site key and sit with
// that site's icon and label.
